\begin{figure}[tbp]
\centering
\resizebox{\linewidth}{!}{\input{fig2_framework.tex}}
\caption{The \HRCOV{} framework. Training phase (top), on validation facts only: the frozen base scores each query, candidate generation forms $C(q)=T_{50}(q)\cup P_B(q)$, features are computed from $\mathcal{H}_{<t}$, the ranker $g_\theta$ is trained with the listwise loss of Eq.~\eqref{eq:loss} on the fit part, and the fusion weights $(\alpha,\beta)$ of Eq.~\eqref{eq:fusion} are calibrated on the selection part. Query phase (bottom): the same pipeline with all learned parts fixed scores each test query; $C(q)$ is ordered by the fused score, the remaining entities follow in base order, and the list is scored by the official time-aware filtered evaluator. \HR{} omits the pattern block.}
\label{fig:framework}
\end{figure}

